questions.question:
Consider the following HEV powertrain controller states:
State 'IDLE': Battery SoC < 10% AND motor torque = 0
State 'BOOST': Battery SoC > 20% AND throttle > 50%

An engineer writes the following C code to evaluate the state machine:

static int gear_pos;
void update_state(int battery_soc, int throttle, int motor_torque) {
    if (battery_soc < 10) {
        if (throttle > 50) {
            gear_pos = 2; // BOOST
        } else {
            gear_pos = 1; // IDLE
        }
    } else {
        gear_pos = 0; // NEUTRAL
    }
}

Given battery_soc = 5, throttle = 60, motor_torque = 0, what value of gear_pos violates the explicitly defined state logic for the IDLE state, and why?

